    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes and the acceptance test is green. The audit log confirms the new format: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and every value derived from it follows.\n\n**Core change \u2014 the customerCode algorithm** (`OwnerIdentities.customerCode`, called by `AssignCustomerCode`):\n- `REGION` = canonical region derived from the postcode (falling back to city) via `Localities.localityFor`.\n- `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (telephone normalized to E.164 exactly as the identity key does).\n- The per-city **sequence numbers are dropped entirely**; `AssignCustomerCode` no longer touches `OwnerRepository` and is now a pure function of the owner.\n\n**Values that moved to the new identity:**\n- **Membership number** (`AssignMembershipNumber`) and its **check digit** (`CheckDigits`) already read `customerCode`, so they automatically produce the new region-and-hash value (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-M26`).\n- **Create audit record** (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now records the new code.\n- **Locality derivation** \u2014 the one that wasn't previously built from the code \u2014 was moved: `OwnerMapper` now calls a new `Localities.localityFor(Owner)` overload that reads the REGION prefix out of the `customerCode` identity (falling back to postcode/city for owners without a code yet, e.g. seed data).\n\nFiles touched: `AssignCustomerCode.java`, `OwnerIdentities.java`, `Localities.java`, `OwnerMapper.java`, plus a doc example in `AssignMembershipNumber.java`.\n\nTest suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The `customerCode` matches the required `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}` shape.",
